===== Return to Factory Firmware =====
Flashing back to Factory Firmware is a quite easy procedure.
You need just run a recovery image from USB Drive in bootloader prompt once.

  - Download the current EdgeRouter recovery image (https://www.ui.com/download/software/er8) from the [[https://help.ui.com/hc/en-us/articles/360019289113-EdgeRouter-TFTP-Recovery|relevant article in Ubiquiti Support and Help Center]] to USB Drive with a single FAT32 partition. \\ //On a Linux system, you can use the following fast script (don't forget to put the right USB device path!):// <code syntax=bash>export USBDRIVE=/dev/sdb1
export TMPDIR=`mktemp -d`
sudo mount $USBDRIVE $TMPDIR -o umask=000
wget -O $TMPDIR/vmlinux.64 https://dl.ui.com/firmwares/edgemax/v2.0.x/ER-e200.recovery.v2.0.6.5208554.190708.0611.16de5fdde.vmlinux.64
sync; sudo umount $USBDRIVE
rmdir $TMPDIR </code>
  - Plug the USB Drive with recovery image to powered off device and do steps 5-10 from [[#easy_installation_via_serial_and_usb|Easy installation via Serial and USB section]].
  - At the bootloader prompt: <code syntax=bash>
# Read the recovery image from USB Drive
Octeon ubnt_e200# usb start
Octeon ubnt_e200# fatload usb 0:1 0x20000000 vmlinux.64
# Boot to recovery image
Octeon ubnt_e200# bootoctlinux 0 </code>
Recovery image will do all necessary actions and after reboot you'll get a default Edgemax firmware.

